From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_VK_OOM_RETRY=<tries>, a descriptor pool the driver refuses with VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY is asked for again a bounded number of times (off unless set)

Why: at the load past Ocarina's field the pool sits at its last MiB for seconds. A draw that needs a
new descriptor pool then ends the app: vkCreateDescriptorPool answers VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY on
the Vulkan worker (Scheduler::WorkerThread, a recorded GraphicsPipeline::ConfigureDraw,
DescriptorAllocator::Commit, ResourcePool::CommitResource, AllocateDescriptors, AllocatePool), and
AllocateDescriptors handles only VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_POOL_MEMORY. run1430 (T177) and run1473 (T184),
symbolized on their own builds. Pairs with the driver's RADV_PS5_INTERNAL_RESERVE_MIB (lead-mesh-46),
which should keep the refusal from happening; this is the backstop when the reserve is empty.

What (src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_descriptor_pool.cpp, AllocatePool only): with
EDEN_UP_VK_OOM_RETRY=<tries> (1 to 50, read once) a refused pool is asked for again up to <tries>
times. Before each try: the front's out-of-memory answer eden_radv_out_of_memory(2 MiB) (headless/
performance.cpp: the heap's empty pages and cold guest memory back to the pool; any thread, memory
work only, nothing that calls back into Vulkan; weak here), then a sleep of 2 ms times the try (20
tries: 420 ms of sleeps, plus each answer's own time: with EDEN_UP_PACK_ON_REFUSAL=1 it may pack up to
64 MiB of guest memory on this thread, 2-5 ms a slot; the worker submits nothing meanwhile, so a wait
reclaim pass waiting for the GPU on the back thread runs out), so the GPU can finish work whose freed memory the driver gives back
and other threads can free theirs. The texture cache's collector and the wait reclaim pass are not
called: they need the GPU thread or the scheduler, and this runs on the worker inside a recorded
command. After the last try the exception goes up as before. Expect a low yield from the answer
itself: at this load every logged eden_radv_out_of_memory call gave back 0 MiB.
Lines (stderr): "EDEN_UP_VK_OOM_RETRY descriptor pool refused (try T of N, R refusals so far): M MiB
given back, trying again", "... descriptor pool made on try T of N (S saved so far)", "... still
refused after T tries: the error goes up" (first 32, then every 64th).

Unset or 0: the switch is read once, at the first pool, and the pool is made outside any try, so a
refusal ends the app from the same frames as T184 (__cxa_throw under CreateDescriptorPool): as T184.
vk_descriptor_pool.cpp is not a translation id input (no file of src/shader_recompiler includes it,
and it is not in tools/gen-translation-id.py's SINGLE list), no header is touched and no name is
added to TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE STORE.

---
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_descriptor_pool.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_descriptor_pool.cpp
index 02b7a32..52cbd64 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_descriptor_pool.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_descriptor_pool.cpp
@@ -5,7 +5,13 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <atomic>
+#include <chrono>
+#include <cstdint>
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <mutex>
+#include <thread>
 #include <span>
 #include <vector>
 
@@ -18,6 +24,11 @@
 #include "video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_device.h"
 #include "video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_wrapper.h"
 
+// EDEN_UP_VK_OOM_RETRY (patch 1070): the front's answer to the driver's out-of-memory (headless/
+// performance.cpp: the heap's empty pages and cold guest memory back to the pool; any thread, memory
+// work only, nothing that calls back into Vulkan). Weak: without the front it is not there.
+extern "C" std::uint64_t eden_radv_out_of_memory(std::uint64_t bytes) __attribute__((weak));
+
 namespace Vulkan {
 
 // Prefer small grow rates to avoid saturating the descriptor pool with barely used pipelines
@@ -82,14 +93,60 @@ static void AllocatePool(const Device& device, DescriptorBank& bank) {
     add(VK_DESCRIPTOR_TYPE_SAMPLED_IMAGE, info.sampled_images);
     add(VK_DESCRIPTOR_TYPE_SAMPLER, info.samplers);
     VideoCommon::Churn::Add(VideoCommon::Churn::DescriptorPools);
-    bank.pools.push_back(device.GetLogical().CreateDescriptorPool({
+    const VkDescriptorPoolCreateInfo create_info{
         .sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_DESCRIPTOR_POOL_CREATE_INFO,
         .pNext = nullptr,
         .flags = 0,
         .maxSets = sets_per_pool,
         .poolSizeCount = static_cast<u32>(pool_cursor),
         .pPoolSizes = std::data(pool_sizes),
-    }));
+    };
+    // EDEN_UP_VK_OOM_RETRY=<tries> (patch 1070, off unless set; 1 to 50): a pool the driver refuses
+    // with VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY is asked for again up to <tries> times, each after the
+    // front's out-of-memory answer (2 MiB asked) and a sleep of 2 ms times the try (sleeps alone:
+    // 5 tries 30 ms, 20 tries 420 ms; with EDEN_UP_PACK_ON_REFUSAL=1 each answer may also pack up
+    // to 64 MiB of guest memory here, 2-5 ms a slot), before the error goes up as before. It runs where the pool is made,
+    // the Vulkan worker inside a recorded draw: the sleeps let the GPU finish work whose freed
+    // memory the driver gives back (radv_ps5_memory_retire) and the other threads free theirs.
+    // Unset or 0: read once at the first pool; the pool is made outside any try, as T184.
+    static const int retries = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_VK_OOM_RETRY");
+        const long tries = value != nullptr ? std::strtol(value, nullptr, 10) : 0;
+        return static_cast<int>(std::clamp<long>(tries, 0, 50));
+    }();
+    if (retries == 0) {
+        // Off: no handler on the way up, so a refusal ends the app from the same frames as T184.
+        bank.pools.push_back(device.GetLogical().CreateDescriptorPool(create_info));
+        return;
+    }
+    for (int attempt = 0;; ++attempt) {
+        try {
+            bank.pools.push_back(device.GetLogical().CreateDescriptorPool(create_info));
+            if (attempt != 0) {
+                static std::atomic<u32> saved{};
+                const u32 count = saved.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed) + 1;
+                if (count <= 32 || count % 64 == 0)
+                    std::fprintf(stderr, "EDEN_UP_VK_OOM_RETRY descriptor pool made on try %d of %d (%u saved so far)\n",
+                                 attempt + 1, retries + 1, count);
+            }
+            return;
+        } catch (const vk::Exception& exception) {
+            if (exception.GetResult() != VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY || attempt >= retries) {
+                if (retries != 0 && exception.GetResult() == VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY)
+                    std::fprintf(stderr, "EDEN_UP_VK_OOM_RETRY descriptor pool still refused after %d tries: the "
+                                 "error goes up\n", attempt + 1);
+                throw;
+            }
+        }
+        const std::uint64_t freed = eden_radv_out_of_memory ? eden_radv_out_of_memory(std::uint64_t{2} << 20) : 0;
+        static std::atomic<u32> refused{};
+        const u32 count = refused.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed) + 1;
+        if (count <= 32 || count % 64 == 0)
+            std::fprintf(stderr, "EDEN_UP_VK_OOM_RETRY descriptor pool refused (try %d of %d, %u refusals so far): "
+                         "%llu MiB given back, trying again\n", attempt + 1, retries + 1, count,
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(freed >> 20));
+        std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(2 * (attempt + 1)));
+    }
 }
 
 DescriptorAllocator::DescriptorAllocator(const Device& device_, MasterSemaphore& master_semaphore_,
